<script data-rh="true" id="seo-schema-1" type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I get a catalog loan on a small catalog?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, companies like Sound Royalties and Lyric Financial offer loans based on verified royalty income streams, even for smaller catalogs. The minimum thresholds vary, but some providers work with catalogs generating as little as $1,000-$5,000 per year."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What interest rates do catalog loans typically carry?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Interest rates for catalog loans typically range from 8-15%, depending on the catalog's revenue consistency, the loan-to-value ratio, the term, and the borrower's overall financial profile. Rates are higher than traditional bank loans because of the asset's specialized nature."}}]}</script>
